  "purpose": "Open interest threshold inputs for Desk A's twelve OICORE wheel places: the settled markets (tickers and times, the reader never reads a result) of 12 fifteen minute series for 2026-10-16 to 2026-11-13T02:35Z, cut around EVENT830's four past forward closes (13:30Z on Nov 5, 6, 10, 12) on its 8 series. The candle job is built from these answers.",
  "heldout": "Development only, ending 2026-11-13T02:35Z (before the NC15 depth-cell places' forward count start 2026-11-13T02:40Z; nothing from it on). Cut out: EVENT830's forward windows, the 13:30Z closes on 2026-11-05, 11-06, 11-10, 11-12 for its 8 series (the 11-13 close is after this window's end) (register: EVENT830 forward read about 2026-12-04, FORWARD READ SCHEDULED); a +-5 minute cut around each close, so no EVENT830 window's result is asked. NC15DEPTH1 pooled scoring opens 2026-11-19T00:00Z, so windows before it are count only and not held out. Other cards that list these series DO hold out dates inside 2026-10-16 to 2026-11-13 (per the registry, Auditor B's reading of Nov 14): PUB20, SETTLE1, SPIKE1, TODSEAS1, VOLSLOT1 (W3 from 2026-10-05), XOI1, TSLM1, QSTALE1, XCRY1, XMET1 (W3 the last third by date count), BOOKCH1 and R6T (XRP forward windows), RESIL1 (XRP, closes from 2026-11-05) and EVENT1 (forward, the six macro series). The settled lists carry a result for every market in these ranges, so the landed run WILL hold results of those cards' held-out windows. Handling: when the run lands it goes into HELDOUT_PULL_RUNS.md (Main, in the same PR as the landing, noting that only tickers and close times are read by the job builder and the structure check); no reader opens it except those two; and the candle builder workers/oicand/oi_candles_job.py reads only ticker and close_time (it reads no result, price or volume field; Auditor B audits it before use). Held-out for the places themselves: HELDOUT_FIRST 2026-12-01T00:00Z.",
